{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Reproduction and fix (2026-11-02 PST, worktree fix-shelduck-timeout)\n\n**Reproduced with a real git process, not only the synthetic result.** A diverged clone where a `pre-merge-commit` hook stalls only `git merge` (fetch stays fast), with the merge's bound set to 1 s:\n\n- Before the fix: the merge was attempted once, killed by the watchdog, aborted, and logged `tickets sync could not auto-merge origin/tickets — local state kept; run: rebar store fsck-recover`. Local commit kept, no MERGE_HEAD left.\n- Control, same stalled merge with a 30 s bound: merges cleanly, no warning. The bound was the only variable.\n- After the fix, bound 1 s: logged `tickets sync: git merge of origin/tickets timed out after 1s and was aborted — local state kept. This is not a merge conflict; the next sync tries again.`\n- After the fix with the fetch bound at 1 s: the same slow merge completes, because merge no longer runs under the fetch bound.\n\n**Change:**\n- `git_outcome.is_watchdog_timeout(result)`: keyed on rc 124 (`WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_RC`), with `\"git timed out after\"` (`WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT_MARKER`, now also the source of that row in `TRANSPORT_RETRIABLE_MARKERS`) as fallback for a non-zero result. Marker tuple contents, buckets and push/fetch retry behaviour are unchanged.\n- `sync._git`: `fetch` keeps `_GIT_TIMEOUT = 30`; every other sync call uses gitutil's existing `_LOCAL_GIT_TIMEOUT = 120`, whose stated purpose is bounding local index mutations. No new timeout value introduced.\n- `sync._union_merge`: aborts as before, then reports a watchdog timeout as a timeout naming the operation and bound; genuine failures keep the `could not auto-merge … fsck-recover` text. Still one attempt; `_with_transient_fault_retry` declines the timeout.\n\n## Audit of the other `run_git_bounded` callers\n\n| Caller | Bound | What a timeout produces | Same class as this bug? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `gitutil.run_git_write` | 120 s local | rc 124 with the timeout text, returned or raised as-is | No |\n| `store_usability._head_resolves` (`rev-parse HEAD`) | 30 s | \"store not usable\"; only reached when the dir has no store structure. O(1) read, so it does not grow with the store | No (a wedged-FS edge, not a scaling misreport) |\n| `event_commit_git._run_git` (add/commit/rm/checkout/reset) | 30 s, pinned equal to push by c2ba | `git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out after 30s` — accurate text | Not a misreport, but the same scaling hazard in the bound: filed as `evolutive-descendent-manta` (discovered_from this ticket), since c2ba chose 30 s deliberately and the trade-off needs a decision |\n| `event_commit_git.run_auto_maintenance` | 120 s local | best-effort, result not surfaced as an error | No |\n| `push._git` (push/fetch) | 30 s | transport bucket, retried | No — network, where the transport bucket is right |\n| `_commands/completion_candidate` | 30 s | `CandidateError(\"<op> failed: git timed out after 30s\")` — accurate, disposable sparse clone | No |\n| `_commands/link_revert` (fetch) | network | a failed refresh is a non-verdict | No |\n\nOnly `sync._union_merge` turned a timeout into a semantic (conflict) verdict; that is the one fixed here.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793669215748108150,"uuid":"015d179d-8a03-4e75-a756-3d75ec2812ef"}